<title>HONG KONG: HK Feb retail sales down three pct in value on yr.</title>
<headline>HK Feb retail sales down three pct in value on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong February retail sales totalled a provisional HK$17.9 billion, down three percent year on year and down 20 percent month on month, Census and Statistics Department figures showed.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value and volume of all retail outlets:</p>
<p>						     Feb	Jan</p>
<p> Total retail sales (on-year)  - value    -3	+15</p>
<p>					 - volume   -7	+10</p>
<p>			  (on-month) - value   -20	**</p>
<p>					 - volume  -20	+2</p>
<p>Breakdown by category (on-year)</p>
<p> Clothing and footwear	   - value   +4	 +14</p>
<p>					 - volume  -4	 +5</p>
<p>Jewellery, watches</p>
<p> clocks, valuable gifts	  - value   +6	 +17</p>
<p>					 - volume +10	 +20</p>
<p>Consumer durables,</p>
<p> excluding cars		    - value   +2	 +4</p>
<p>					 - volume  **	 +3</p>
<p> Department stores		 - value   -1	 +9</p>
<p>					 - volume  -7	 +3</p>
<p> Supermarkets			- value   +6	 +13</p>
<p>					 - volume  **	 +6</p>
<p> Fuels				 - value   +9	 +11</p>
<p>					 - volume  +1	 +4</p>
<p> Motor vehicles		    - value   +38	+71</p>
<p>					 - volume  +38	+71</p>
<p>Food, alcoholic drinks and</p>
<p> tobacco			     - value   +3	 +6</p>
<p>					 - volume  **	 +2</p>
<p>** = virtually unchanged</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
